					"font-size": {
						"type": "number",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "text",
						"value": "STRING\nWire has two string nodes. The string input node (top in the example) will take a string from Resolume and put it into Wire.  The collection string (bottom) is made in Wire and will stay in Wire. Use the input node if you want your user to input a string, use the collection node for internal uses. The collection string can also be used to convert floats, booleans and integers to strings.\n\nExample: Two string nodes are combined using the concatenate node before being renderd out.\nBelow that we are using a String node to convert a float into a string."
					}
				},
